 "digits_note": "Significant digits trusted. 45 = conservative cap: dps-50 vs dps-70 runs agree to 49.6-51.0 digits (limited by the dps-50 run), and matching points u_m=0.5 vs 0.6 at dps 70 agree to all 70 digits. d=3,qbar=1: exactly -3/2 (= -i*2*pi*T) by a two-sided enclosure of the continuous branch, width 1.0e-34.",
 "branch_check": "Each d: started at qbar=0.05 with seed gamma=qbar^2 and continued in steps of 0.05 to 1.5 (secant, seeded from the previous roots). At every 0.1 in qbar, F(gamma) (real for omega=-i*gamma) was sign-scanned on (0, max(6, 3*gamma)] (120 linear + 40 geometric points down to 5e-4). At every scanned qbar for every d, exactly one purely imaginary zero exists in that window, and it equals the continued root. So the reported pole is the unique purely damped mode below 3*gamma, connected continuously to omega ~ -i qbar^2. The small-qbar limit is checked at qbar=0.02 for d=3, 4, 5.5: gamma - (qbar^2 + H_{2/d} qbar^4/d) = 7.2e-12, 2.2e-12, 4.7e-13, which is O(qbar^6)=6.4e-11. d=3 hits the n=1 pole-skipping point at qbar=1 (qbar^2=(d-1)/2, gamma=d/2), where F vanishes identically. There, gamma(1-+1e-35) = 1.5 -+ 5.088049691499223e-35 at dps 80, with u_m=0.5 and 0.6 agreeing, and both sides have slope 5.0880496914992230265. Independent double-precision cross-check, integrating the original EF Z equation directly: d=3 qbar=1.5 7.59371434426 (vs 7.59371434395), d=4 qbar=1 1.19613147403337, d=5 qbar=1 1.11539088334707.",
 "control_d4": "d=4, qbar=1 => q=2, 2*pi*T=d/2=2, so frak w = Omega/2 and frak q = 1. Computed Omega = -1.1961314740333803090049625724408950831576512085376 i => frak w = -0.59806573701669015450248128622 i. Kovtun-Starinets hep-th/0506184 (TeX quasisound-v2.tex l.2097-2099): frak w = -0.598066 i for the shear mode at frak q = 1. Agrees to all 6 published digits. Same code, complex omega, first non-hydro shear mode: frak w = 1.75911558480393 - 1.29159379723280 i vs KS table (l.2133) +-1.759116 - 1.291594 i. Agrees.",
